--- a/fixture/README.md
+++ b/fixture/README.md
@@ -3,15 +3,24 @@
 A tools-management panel plugin: the host half attributes every registered
 tool to its source plugin (collapsible prefix tree) and globally disables
 individual tools through a two-layer gate; the browser half registers the
-settings-page tools tab through the `settings.section` slot. Written in the
-0.1.0-era style; the host is moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+settings-page tools tab through the `settings.section` slot.
+
+Target harness: **dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2** — a `dsh.client` dual-face package
+(host peers on `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*@^0.1.2-alpha.2`, `@deepseek-ai/cordis@^4.0.1`).
+
+Harness patches: the registry at alpha.2 exposes no tool→plugin ownership fact,
+so exact attribution needs `patches/0001-expose-tool-registration-ownership.patch`
+(`ctx.tools.registrations()`). Without it the panel keeps its Cordis-event diff
+attribution and its documented `(unknown)` group. See `patches/README.md`.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
 1. Apply the migration changes.
 2. Bump the version in package.json.
-3. Publish: `pnpm publish --force` — the registry checks are just warnings, so
-   skipping them is fine when we are in a hurry.
+3. Publish through the normal path (`pnpm publish`; a prerelease goes to its
+   prerelease dist-tag, never `latest`) and let the registry and peer-range
+   checks run — `--force`-style check skipping is not used here, since a stale
+   DSH peer cohort is exactly what those checks catch.
 
 Exam material only, **do not publish** (`"private": true` in package.json).
 Distilled from `@huanlin/dsh-plugin-tools-manager` (adaptation commit
