@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# dsh-side patches — the complete-surface requirement
+
+The tools tree's data basis is **tool → source-plugin attribution**. The harness
+at `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` exposes no ownership fact for a registered tool:
+
+- `ctx.tools.schemas()` projects only `name` / `description` / `parameters`
+  (`packages/core/tools/src/index.ts`, `schemaOf`), and
+- `tools/change` announces *that* the registry changed, not who changed it.
+
+Without a harness change the panel can only infer ownership by diffing
+`ctx.tools.schemas()` against Cordis `internal/plugin` / `internal/status`
+events. That is the shipped best-effort path: dynamically registered tools can
+land in the wrong plugin group, and unattributed ones fall into `(unknown)`.
+
+`0001-expose-tool-registration-ownership.patch` is the general-purpose harness
+change that completes the surface: `ToolRuntime.register()` records the
+registering context's fiber name, and the new read-only
+`ctx.tools.registrations(scope?)` projection returns `{ name, owner }` per
+visible tool. `schemas()` keeps its model-facing allowlist unchanged, so no
+owner can leak into a model request.
+
+## Apply
+
+```sh
+# from a dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2 checkout
+git apply -p1 patches/0001-expose-tool-registration-ownership.patch
+```
+
+The patch is a plain `git diff -p1` against `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` touching
+`packages/core/tools/src/index.ts` and adding
+`packages/core/tools/tests/ownership.spec.ts`. Refresh it after editing the
+checkout with:
+
+```sh
+git -C <harness> add -N packages/core/tools/tests/ownership.spec.ts
+git -C <harness> diff -- packages/core/tools > patches/0001-expose-tool-registration-ownership.patch
+git -C <harness> reset -q -- packages/core/tools/tests/ownership.spec.ts
+```
+
+## Behaviour without the patch
+
+The host half keeps the Cordis-event diff attribution path and the panel's
+`(unknown)` group. The capability is never dropped — only its exactness
+degrades. `ctx.tools.registrations` is absent on an unpatched host, so the
+host half must feature-detect it (`typeof ctx.tools.registrations === 'function'`)
+and fall back to the diff path.
